                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Flagstaff AZ",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued August 25 at 5:19AM MST until August 25 at 9:00AM MST by NWS Flagstaff AZ",
                "description": "FFWFGZ\n\nThe National Weather Service in Flagstaff has extended the\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nThe Paria River in...\nCoconino County in north central Arizona...\n\n* Until 900 AM MST /1000 AM MDT/.\n\n* At 519 AM MST /619 AM MDT/, a river gauge on the Paria River\nreported a rapid rise of 5 feet from thunderstorms on Monday. Flash\nflooding is already occurring.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding in and around the Paria\nRiver.\n\nSOURCE...River gauge reported.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of areas in and around the\nParia River.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nVermilion Cliffs National Monument and Lees Ferry.\n\nThis includes the Colorado River near mile marker 0.\n\nThis includes the following recreation areas and campgrounds...\nLees Ferry Camp Site.\n\nThis includes the following creeks, washes and rivers...\nParia River and Colorado River.",
                "instruction": "Get out of the Paria River slot canyon! Flood waters will flow down\nthe Paria River, reaching the confluence with the Colorado River at\nLees Ferry between 7 AM and 8 AM MST.",
                "response": "Avoid",
